WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.161
Hey everybody, it's Craig Thomas.
大家好，我是克雷格·托马斯。

00:00:02.161 --> 00:00:10.839
I wrote a book and I want you to know about it, but instead of watching me or listening to me be self-promotional in a blatant and uncomfortable way.
我写了一本书，我想让你知道它，但不要以一种公然和不舒服的方式自我推销，而不是看我或听我。

00:00:10.839 --> 00:00:13.507
I was delighted by this book.
我对这本书感到很高兴。

00:00:13.507 --> 00:00:15.623
It is super page-turny.
这是超级翻页的。

00:00:15.623 --> 00:00:20.039
It is like breathlessly and hilariously plotted.
这就像令人窒息且滑稽的情节。

00:00:20.039 --> 00:00:25.879
The interiority was just as rich and as fun as the plot twists.
内在的内容和情节的曲折一样丰富和有趣。

00:00:25.879 --> 00:00:31.079
His many years of crafting great narratives on television came to bear on this.
他多年来在电视上精心制作的精彩故事对此产生了影响。

00:00:31.079 --> 00:00:33.759
Your gifts as a novelist are just abundant.
你作为小说家的天赋非常丰富。

00:00:33.759 --> 00:00:35.240
I was so delighted by it.
我对此感到非常高兴。

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:36.920
It's incredibly vivid.
它非常生动。

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:39.200
You're really seeing it as you read it.
当你阅读它时，你确实看到了它。

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.920
Even if you were my mortal enemy, I would be forced to.
就算你是我的死敌，我也不得不这么做。

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:42.759
I'd love you dearly.
我会深深地爱你。

00:00:42.759 --> 00:00:47.399
You're one of my best friends, but I would be forced to concede that you had written a great book.
你是我最好的朋友之一，但我不得不承认你写了一本很棒的书。

00:00:47.399 --> 00:00:48.369
That is amazing.
这真是太棒了。

00:00:48.369 --> 00:00:53.399
I wish that could be a blurb on the book, even if Frank Thomas was my mortal enemy.
我希望这能成为书中的一个简介，即使弗兰克·托马斯是我的死敌。

00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:59.000
You will not be disappointed if you pick up this book or listen to this book, so check it out.
如果你拿起这本书或听这本书，你不会失望的，所以请看一下。

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.454
And speaking of listening to this book, there is a mini How I Met Your Mother reunion in the audiobook of That's Not How It Happened.
说到听这本书，在《That's Not How It Happened》的有声书中有一个迷你《老爸老妈的浪漫史》重聚。

00:01:06.454 --> 00:01:07.799
Listen to Kobe Smoltres.
听听科比·斯莫尔特雷斯的声音。

00:01:07.799 --> 00:01:15.799
And so began the surreal, unholy process of my husband adapting my book, My Life, into a screenplay.
于是，我丈夫将我的书《我的生活》改编成剧本，开始了超现实、邪恶的过程。

00:01:15.799 --> 00:01:19.480
Here's another voice you may recognize, Josh Redder.
这是您可能认识的另一个声音，乔什·雷德。

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:21.706
Right now, I was in that pocket.
现在，我就在那个口袋里。

00:01:21.706 --> 00:01:25.879
And as a writer, that's about as close to heaven as it gets.
作为一名作家，这几乎是最接近天堂的了。

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:28.484
Okay, self-promotion over.
好了，自我推销结束了。

00:01:28.484 --> 00:01:30.359
Now to this week's episode.
现在到本周的剧集。

00:01:30.359 --> 00:01:31.400
It's a big one.
这是一个很大的。

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:35.079
Ladies and gentlemen, how we met Neil Patrick Harris.
女士们先生们，我们是如何认识尼尔·帕特里克·哈里斯的。

00:01:49.099 --> 00:01:55.739
me to tell you everything in New York City.
我来告诉你纽约市的一切。

00:01:55.739 --> 00:02:00.540
Hello and welcome to another episode of How We Made Your Mother.
大家好，欢迎收看《我们如何成就了你的母亲》的另一集。

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:04.260
I'm Josh Ratner, your co-host, my other co-host.
我是乔什·拉特纳，你的搭档主持人，也是我的另一位搭档主持人。

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:05.700
I'm staring at his hands and face.
我盯着他的手和脸。

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:06.819
Now his name's Craig Thomas.
现在他的名字是克雷格·托马斯。

00:02:06.819 --> 00:02:07.579
Hi, Craig.
嗨，克雷格。

00:02:07.579 --> 00:02:07.980
Why?
为什么？

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:09.020
I'm blushing, sir.
我脸红了，先生。

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:10.099
Thank you.
谢谢。

00:02:10.099 --> 00:02:11.340
Do I not call you handsome enough?
我还嫌你不够帅吗？

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:12.419
Not really enough.
还不够。

00:02:12.419 --> 00:02:13.620
It's implied.
这是暗示的。

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:15.900
I'm always feeling it.
我一直有这种感觉。

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:18.780
We made a TV show together years ago.
几年前我们一起制作了一个电视节目。

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:21.020
It started what, 20, 19 years ago.
事情要从20、19年前开始说起。

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:22.620
It was called How I Met Your Mother.
它的名字叫《老爸老妈的浪漫史》。

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.060
We did 208 episodes.
我们拍了208集。

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:26.699
It ran from 2005 to 2014.
它从2005年持续到2014年。

00:02:26.699 --> 00:02:27.939
We haven't seen it in years.
我们已经很多年没见过它了。

00:02:27.939 --> 00:02:32.740
We're going back through every single episode with our older, wiser eyes.
我们将用更年长、更明智的眼光回顾每一集。

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:35.539
We're very proud of what we made for the most part.
我们对我们所做的大部分工作感到非常自豪。

00:02:35.539 --> 00:02:37.860
And yeah, we're having a great time.
是的，我们玩得很开心。

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:40.819
And we always say this is a special episode.
我们总是说这是一个特别的插曲。

00:02:40.819 --> 00:02:41.939
This is a special episode.
这是一个特别的情节。

00:02:41.939 --> 00:02:53.860
This isn't just such a special extra, extra special episode Because we have a man here who, it's just impossible to imagine the world of how I met your mother without.
这不仅仅是一个特别的特别特别的插曲，因为我们这里有一个男人，如果没有他，我根本无法想象我是如何遇见你母亲的世界。

00:02:53.860 --> 00:03:01.620
He is the person who breathed life into the great iconic Barney Stinson and his name is Neil Patrick Harrison.
他为伟大的标志性人物巴尼·斯汀森注入了生命，他的名字叫尼尔·帕特里克·哈里森。

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:02.620
He's with us today.
今天他和我们在一起。

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:03.939
What?
什么？

00:03:03.939 --> 00:03:04.939
What?
什么？

00:03:04.939 --> 00:03:05.780
Hey, Neil.
嘿，尼尔。

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:07.979
Please sit down, please, everyone sit.
请坐，请大家坐下。

00:03:07.979 --> 00:03:11.060
What's up, man?
怎么了，伙计？

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:11.900
Thank you.
谢谢。

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:12.740
Good to see you.
很高兴见到你。

00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:14.900
It's nice to see your smiling faces.
很高兴看到你们的笑脸。

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:17.360
Oh my gosh, Alec as well.
哦天哪，还有亚历克。

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:19.139
Thank you for being here, buddy.
谢谢你来到这里，伙计。

00:03:19.139 --> 00:03:21.979
What have you been doing since 2014?
自2014年以来你在做什么？

00:03:21.979 --> 00:03:22.939
How have you been?
你最近怎么样？

00:03:24.539 --> 00:03:26.139
I've been good, hookin'.
我一直很好，很迷恋。

00:03:26.139 --> 00:03:29.139
I saw you, I saw your, you won a Tony, I saw that.
我看到了你，我看到了你，你赢得了托尼奖，我看到了。

00:03:29.139 --> 00:03:33.219
I remember you jumped on my seat in the audience and you kissed me, I believe on the mouth.
我记得你在观众席上跳到我的座位上，然后吻了我，我相信是在嘴上。

00:03:33.219 --> 00:03:34.060
For sure.
一定。

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:36.139
I think I got glitter on my face.
我想我的脸上闪闪发光。

00:03:36.139 --> 00:03:37.620
Well, we had already, we'll talk about that.
好吧，我们已经讨论过了，我们会讨论这个。

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:39.819
We had already broken that.
我们已经打破了这一点。

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:44.939
And so you're living in New York City And let me just start with this.
你住在纽约市 让我从这个开始。

00:03:44.939 --> 00:03:54.740
We talk about how the tale of this show, there were shows that were so popular when we were on the air, that people just do not talk about anymore.
我们谈论这个节目的故事，当我们播出时，有些节目非常受欢迎，但人们不再谈论了。

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:59.240
But for some reason, How I Met Your Mother is still very much in the zeitgeist, it's still in the culture.
但出于某种原因，《老爸老妈浪漫史》仍然很符合时代精神，仍然属于文化。

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:02.699
People still reference it, talk about it, discover it anew.
人们仍然引用它、谈论它、重新发现它。

00:04:02.699 --> 00:04:10.620
So I'm just curious, in your day-to-day life, you get recognized for a lot of things, but what's your experience of meeting how I met your mother fans?
所以我很好奇，在你的日常生活中，你会因为很多事情而得到认可，但是你遇到我遇到你妈妈粉丝的经历是什么？

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:18.860
and how has the show kind of changed in your perception of it as you've gotten more time away from it?
随着你远离这部剧的时间越来越多，你对它的看法发生了怎样的变化？

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:20.779
Wow, an interesting question.
哇，一个有趣的问题。

00:04:20.779 --> 00:04:34.139
It's been constant, I mean, really, truly constant because when we did our final season, the show was on more times per day than ever.
我的意思是，它一直是恒定的，真的，真正恒定的，因为当我们制作最后一季时，该节目每天播放的次数比以往任何时候都多。

00:04:34.139 --> 00:04:37.899
So it was on three or four times a day in America.
所以在美国每天播放三四次。

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:46.259
And then when Netflix picked it up, it had another resurgence, and then it went somewhere else, then Netflix picked it up again, it had another resurgence.
然后，当 Netflix 接手它时，它再次复兴，然后它去了其他地方，然后 Netflix 再次接手它，它再次复兴。

00:04:46.259 --> 00:04:56.980
Now, you know, I have my husband and I have twin 14-year-old children and their friends are watching it now, they're from high school.
现在，你知道，我有我的丈夫，我有一对 14 岁的双胞胎孩子，他们的朋友现在正在观看它，他们来自高中。

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:58.220
Are they watching it at Harper and Gideon watch it?
他们在哈珀和吉迪恩那里看吗？

00:04:58.220 --> 00:04:59.860
Yeah, for sure, so.
是的，当然，所以。

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:00.699
Oh my God.
我的天啊。

00:05:00.699 --> 00:05:25.339
So that's interesting because now that's a whole other level of like celebrity dynamic, but in a strange direction, because, you know, I want Harper and Gideon to be identified independently and they have their own, you know, triggers and issues with potentially only being recognized as the child of Barney Stinson.
所以这很有趣，因为现在这是一个完全不同的名人动态水平，但方向很奇怪，因为，你知道，我希望哈珀和吉迪恩能够被独立识别，他们有自己的，你知道的，触发因素和问题，可能只能被认为是巴尼·斯廷森的孩子。

00:05:25.339 --> 00:05:27.740
It's a complicated legacy.
这是一个复杂的遗产。

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:28.740
Yeah, for sure.
是的，当然。

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:32.339
It's a good and bad and it's something that they'll have to process.
这有好有坏，这是他们必须处理的事情。

00:05:32.339 --> 00:05:45.660
But I've had some really great marker chapters professionally in my life since then that have been super great and recognizable and fulfilling as well.
但从那时起，我在职业生涯中经历了一些非常伟大的标记章节，这些章节非常伟大、可识别且令人满意。

00:05:45.660 --> 00:06:04.877
But boy, yeah, people keep coming back to Barney and I'm so appreciative of it and I'm so grateful for the show because especially having played Barney, he was intended to be kind of the fifth wheel life of the party guy that you want to buy a drink and buy the next round and go on some crazy acid venture, right?
但是天哪，是的，人们不断回到巴尼，我对此非常感激，我非常感谢这个节目，因为特别是扮演巴尼之后，他本打算成为派对家伙的第五轮生活，你想买一杯饮料，买下一轮，然后继续一些疯狂的迷幻冒险，对吧？

00:06:04.877 --> 00:06:08.060
That was how he was going to construct it, it seems.
看来他就是打算这样建造它的。

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:30.582
And so when I meet people who love the show, they're very positive and they're very enthusiastic and they have specifics and they tell me about the playbook and how many that they tried and that they met their girl doing the naked man and that they've been to the Liberty Bell, like, you know, it's, and a lot of people say that they have watched the show eight times.
所以当我遇到喜欢这个节目的人时，他们非常积极，他们非常热情，他们有具体细节，他们告诉我剧本和他们尝试了多少，他们遇到了他们的女孩在做裸体男人，他们去过自由钟，就像，你知道的，很多人说他们已经看过这个节目八次了。

00:06:30.582 --> 00:06:31.082
Yeah.
是的。

00:06:31.082 --> 00:06:32.306
All the way through.
一路走过去。

00:06:32.306 --> 00:06:38.855
Do you ever have the experience that they're bringing up something that you're like, I don't remember that.
你是否有过这样的经历，他们提出了一些你喜欢的东西，我不记得了。

00:06:38.855 --> 00:06:43.873
Like they're they did something so specific, like they just watched it last night.
就像他们做了一些非常具体的事情，就像他们昨晚刚刚看过一样。

00:06:43.873 --> 00:06:47.607
And you're like, I barely remember what you're talking about.
你说，我几乎不记得你在说什么。

00:06:47.607 --> 00:06:48.158
For sure.
一定。

00:06:48.158 --> 00:06:55.073
And and especially when someone comes up and they were on in the show, in an episode that had four or five lines.
尤其是当有人出现并且他们出现在节目中时，在一集有四五句台词的节目中。

00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:59.800
You had a really awkward thing with Joe Manganello, you're like, I don't know this guy.
你和乔·曼加内罗之间发生了一件非常尴尬的事情，你会说，我不认识这个人。

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:02.439
I haven't seen you before in my life.
我一生中从未见过你。

00:07:02.439 --> 00:07:03.439
But wow, look at your arms.
但是哇，看看你的手臂。

00:07:03.439 --> 00:07:05.600
And he takes his shirt off and you're like, oh, I remember this guy.
他脱掉衬衫，你就会说，哦，我记得这个人。

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:06.439
Oh yeah, that guy.
哦，是的，那个家伙。

00:07:08.079 --> 00:07:12.040
So no, it's just been, it's just been a delight.
所以不，这只是，这只是一种乐趣。

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:15.399
It weirdly, I'm 52 years old, you know?
奇怪的是，我已经52岁了，你知道吗？

00:07:15.399 --> 00:07:26.079
And people still consider me, will treat me as if I'm like vibrant, let's go have a great time and do fun things together.
人们仍然会考虑我，会对待我，就好像我充满活力一样，让我们​​一起去享受美好时光，一起做有趣的事情吧。

00:07:26.079 --> 00:07:27.079
Yeah.
是的。

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:27.920
And that's fun.
这很有趣。

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:36.920
Like it's fun to not be like the dusty older sage, but instead to still be like the one that can be devilish.
不像那位尘土飞扬的老圣人，而是仍然像一个邪恶的人，这很有趣。

00:07:36.920 --> 00:07:38.720
It was a devilish part.
这是一个邪恶的部分。

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:46.240
And I'm so grateful, Craig, to you and Carter, mostly to you, just because Carter's not here right now.
克雷格，我非常感谢你和卡特，主要是感谢你，只是因为卡特现在不在这里。

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:47.720
The feeling is very mutual.
这种感觉是非常相互的。

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:52.120
Neil, I don't want to, I'm struggling with how much are a little too embarrassed to you during this.
尼尔，我不想，我正在挣扎，在这期间我对你有点太尴尬了。

00:07:52.120 --> 00:08:02.399
But like each, every single episode we've done and we're at the end of season two almost now, every week we're saying like, how the fuck did Neil do that physical comedy thing or how did you find that moment?
但就像我们完成的每一集一样，现在第二季已经快结束了，每周我们都会说，尼尔到底是怎么做到那个肢体喜剧的，或者你是怎么找到那个时刻的？

00:08:02.399 --> 00:08:05.639
How, how does he do that turn on a dime the way he does?
怎么样，他是怎么做到像他那样的？

00:08:05.639 --> 00:08:09.879
There's, we're, we're, we're fanning out on you a bunch rewatching our own show that we all made together.
我们、我们、我们正在向你们散开，让你们重温我们共同制作的节目。

00:08:09.879 --> 00:08:10.879
So I just wanted to say that.
所以我只想这么说。

00:08:10.879 --> 00:08:11.879
Thank you, man.
谢谢你，伙计。

00:08:11.879 --> 00:08:17.680
It was, it was one of those rare gifts that I'm sure you have talked about ad nauseam.
这是，我相信你已经谈得津津有味的稀有礼物之一。

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:24.480
where it was such a hybrid show at a time when that really didn't exist.
这是一场混合表演，而当时这种表演实际上并不存在。

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:43.740
And so we were doing a multi-camera show with no audience as if there was an audience, and we were able to cut and reset and restart, and we were helmed by Pam Fryman, who was such like a heartbeat truthful sensor for everyone in their own ways, always.
因此，我们正在做一场没有观众的多机位表演，就好像有观众一样，我们能够剪切、重置和重新开始，我们由帕姆·弗莱曼（Pam Fryman）掌舵，他总是以自己的方式为每个人提供心跳真实的传感器。

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:48.803
And that North Star, I think, allowed everyone freedom to try shit and fail.
我认为，北极星让每个人都有尝试和失败的自由。

00:08:48.803 --> 00:09:02.862
And the stuff that, I mean, I just felt like it was this back and forth between team writers room and team actor is they would sort of challenge us with like what, let's see if they, if this would be successful.
我的意思是，我只是觉得团队编剧室和团队演员之间来来回回，他们会用什么来挑战我们，让我们看看他们是否会成功。

00:09:02.862 --> 00:10:00.628
And when it came to the Barney stuff, because, you know, Josh was so exquisite at the, at the pathos part and at making a laugh-tracked 22 minutes feel so sort of cinematic and real that then I was sort of gifted all of like the craziness and I was so fun to do because if it was a real sitcom with a multi-camera live studio audience it's a very different experience you rehearse all week and then it's show night and you really only have a couple cracks at it you do it and then you huddle up and the audience laughed at it, but they didn't laugh like you thought, so you write a bunch of stuff and then the guy is upstairs telling them, I'll give you chocolates if you laugh louder, and so then the second time you do it, it's like really big responses for everything and they're wanting to hear themselves when they go home later, so that's just a different vibe.
当谈到巴尼的东西时，因为，你知道，乔什在悲伤的部分和让笑声不断的 22 分钟感觉如此电影和真实，然后我有点像疯狂的天赋，我很有趣，因为如果这是一部真正的情景喜剧，有多个镜头现场演播室观众，那是一种非常不同的体验，你排练了一整周，然后到了演出之夜，你真的只有几个裂缝如果你这样做，然后你挤在一起，观众就会笑，但他们不像你想象的那样笑，所以你写了一堆东西，然后楼上的那个人告诉他们，如果你笑得更大声，我会给你巧克力，所以当你第二次这样做时，就像对所有事情都有很大的反应，他们想稍后回家时听到自己的声音，所以这只是一种不同的氛围。

00:10:00.628 --> 00:10:03.559
We were able to do things five or six times.
我们能够做五六次事情。

00:10:03.559 --> 00:10:04.919
